{
  "case_id": "2007-06-637",
  "document_hash": "21c38fa5db99922f4ebbcfed11defcbd2709ebc5bf99889894b0b2e5bfa63ae2",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2007-06-637",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "21c38fa5db99922f4ebbcfed11defcbd2709ebc5bf99889894b0b2e5bfa63ae2",
      "evidence_id": "ev-21c38fa5db99-0000-0000",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 1,
        "start": 1
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "LEONARD J. KOERNER, ESQ., New York, N.Y.; on behalf of\nPetitioner.\nPAUL G. GARDEPHE, ESQ., New York, N.Y.; on behalf of\nRespondent.\nGREGORY G. GARRE, ESQ., Deputy Solicitor General,\nDepartment of Justice, Washington, D.C.; on\nbehalf of the United States, as amicus curiae,\nsupporting Respondents."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Leonard J. Koerner",
      "case_id": "2007-06-637",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "21c38fa5db99922f4ebbcfed11defcbd2709ebc5bf99889894b0b2e5bfa63ae2",
      "evidence_id": "ev-21c38fa5db99-0000-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. KOERNER: Mr. Chief Justice, and members\nof the Court. In 1985 when this Court decided the\nBurlington decision, it based -- it based it based on\nthe broad remedial clause set forth in 20 U.S.C. 1415,\nwhich allowed an impartial hearing officer, a state\nreview officer, or the court, itself, to grant relief\nwhere appropriate.\nIn so doing, it noted that there was no\nother substantive section which touched and concerned\nthe issue before the Court, and that is whether an\nindividual can voluntarily remove a child and seek\ntuition reimbursement before the conclusion of the\nadministrative and court remedies."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2007-06-637",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "21c38fa5db99922f4ebbcfed11defcbd2709ebc5bf99889894b0b2e5bfa63ae2",
      "evidence_id": "ev-21c38fa5db99-0000-0003",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 6,
        "start": 6
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "which is adequate, you cannot get reimbursement if you\nremove your child during any time but in this case\nduring the pendency of the administrative and the court\nprocess."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2007-06-637",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "21c38fa5db99922f4ebbcfed11defcbd2709ebc5bf99889894b0b2e5bfa63ae2",
      "evidence_id": "ev-21c38fa5db99-0000-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 7,
        "start": 7
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: If Gilbert F. had attended the public school for 11 days, would this case come out\ndifferently, in your view?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2007-06-637",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "21c38fa5db99922f4ebbcfed11defcbd2709ebc5bf99889894b0b2e5bfa63ae2",
      "evidence_id": "ev-21c38fa5db99-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 19,
        "start": 19
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: Is there any suggestion in the reasoning in the Burlington case that it was limited to a situation in which the student had been receiving public school special education?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Solicitor General",
      "case_id": "2007-06-637",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "21c38fa5db99922f4ebbcfed11defcbd2709ebc5bf99889894b0b2e5bfa63ae2",
      "evidence_id": "ev-21c38fa5db99-0001-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 19,
        "start": 19
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The second argument that is made both by the Solicitor General and Respondent is that there's been an -- implied repeals of this Court's decisions in Burlington and Carter."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2007-06-637",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "21c38fa5db99922f4ebbcfed11defcbd2709ebc5bf99889894b0b2e5bfa63ae2",
      "evidence_id": "ev-21c38fa5db99-0001-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 22,
        "start": 22
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: What is the basis for saying that, when the one thing that the statute is very clear on is that the starting premise of any reimbursement claim is that an appropriate public education is not available?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2007-06-637",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "21c38fa5db99922f4ebbcfed11defcbd2709ebc5bf99889894b0b2e5bfa63ae2",
      "evidence_id": "ev-21c38fa5db99-0001-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 23,
        "start": 23
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BREYER: What about an exception if, in fact, the school district admits that they can't do anything for this child?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2007-06-637",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "21c38fa5db99922f4ebbcfed11defcbd2709ebc5bf99889894b0b2e5bfa63ae2",
      "evidence_id": "ev-21c38fa5db99-0001-0006",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 26,
        "start": 26
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SCALIA: What did it do, then? What meaning do you give to it?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2007-06-637",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "21c38fa5db99922f4ebbcfed11defcbd2709ebc5bf99889894b0b2e5bfa63ae2",
      "evidence_id": "ev-21c38fa5db99-0001-0007",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 27,
        "start": 27
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SCALIA: Where else does it say that the city will pay for the cost of a private education except there? That's the only place it says it. And part of the requirements for getting it is that the child was receiving service at a public institution."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2007-06-637",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "21c38fa5db99922f4ebbcfed11defcbd2709ebc5bf99889894b0b2e5bfa63ae2",
      "evidence_id": "ev-21c38fa5db99-0001-0010",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 30,
        "start": 30
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: In that case, isn't it pertinent that the title to (C)(ii) says \"Reimbursement for Private School Placement\"? It doesn't say reimbursement for private school placement when the child previously attended public school."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2007-06-637",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "21c38fa5db99922f4ebbcfed11defcbd2709ebc5bf99889894b0b2e5bfa63ae2",
      "evidence_id": "ev-21c38fa5db99-0001-0011",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 31,
        "start": 31
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: Where is that set forth?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2007-06-637",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "21c38fa5db99922f4ebbcfed11defcbd2709ebc5bf99889894b0b2e5bfa63ae2",
      "evidence_id": "ev-21c38fa5db99-0001-0012",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 32,
        "start": 32
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: Were those provisions at issue when this dispute arose? They are the 2004 amendments --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "United States (Amicus Curiae)",
      "case_id": "2007-06-637",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "21c38fa5db99922f4ebbcfed11defcbd2709ebc5bf99889894b0b2e5bfa63ae2",
      "evidence_id": "ev-21c38fa5db99-0002-0004",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. GARDEPHE: The point we are trying to make, Your Honor, is that in light of Burlington, which obviously Congress had knowledge of when it enacted the 1997 amendments, is it credible to believe that they would have restricted, limited, overruled the holding of Burlington, and never said a word about it?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2007-06-637",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "21c38fa5db99922f4ebbcfed11defcbd2709ebc5bf99889894b0b2e5bfa63ae2",
      "evidence_id": "ev-21c38fa5db99-0002-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 44,
        "start": 44
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. GARRE: Thank you, Mr. Chief Justice, and may it please the Court:\nPetitioner takes the position that a school district may both refuse to provide a child with a disability with an appropriate public placement and refuse to pay for an appropriate private placement."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2007-06-637",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "21c38fa5db99922f4ebbcfed11defcbd2709ebc5bf99889894b0b2e5bfa63ae2",
      "evidence_id": "ev-21c38fa5db99-0002-0003",
      "kind": "stated_consequence",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 53,
        "start": 53
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "courts have equitable discretion to deny reimbursement claims, and they have denied those reimbursement claims."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2007-06-637",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "21c38fa5db99922f4ebbcfed11defcbd2709ebc5bf99889894b0b2e5bfa63ae2",
      "evidence_id": "ev-21c38fa5db99-0003-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 54,
        "start": 54
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "During the period between Burlington and the enactment of this statute, would you have any doubt about your potential obligation to reimburse a parent -- during the period of Burlington and the enactment of the statute, would the school board"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Koerner",
      "case_id": "2007-06-637",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "21c38fa5db99922f4ebbcfed11defcbd2709ebc5bf99889894b0b2e5bfa63ae2",
      "evidence_id": "ev-21c38fa5db99-0003-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 55,
        "start": 55
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "No, the -- this is just a grant provision, Your Honor. It's not premised on any constitutional provision. It's a grant where funds are provided to the local education district, and in return they agree to comply with all the conditions set forth in the IDEA. There are no constitutional limits."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2007-06-637",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "21c38fa5db99922f4ebbcfed11defcbd2709ebc5bf99889894b0b2e5bfa63ae2",
      "evidence_id": "ev-21c38fa5db99-0003-0002",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 56,
        "start": 56
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The case is submitted. (Whereupon, at 11:55 a.m. the case in the above-entitled matter was submitted.)"
    },
    {
